{%- comment -%}
  Cart count for the header cart link (docs/BUILD.md 6.1 and 6.7). Two siblings, so
  the header__cart flex layout is the same as before:
    - the accessible text, "Carrito, N productos", read with the link;
    - the visible number, hidden from assistive technology (the text already says it) and
      hidden entirely when the cart is empty.

  JavaScript hooks: the listener in assets/core.js updates both on mares:cart:updated.
  The singular and plural sentences are rendered here, with [count] in place of the
  number, so the script only picks one and puts a number in it; it never writes copy.
  Without the script the count is what the server rendered on this page load.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cart-count' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

<span
  class="visually-hidden"
  data-cart-count-label
  data-text-one="{{ 'accessibility.cart_count.one' | t: count: '[count]' }}"
  data-text-other="{{ 'accessibility.cart_count.other' | t: count: '[count]' }}"
>
  {{- 'accessibility.cart_count' | t: count: cart.item_count -}}
</span>
<span class="header__cart-count text-body-sm" aria-hidden="true" data-cart-count{% if cart.item_count == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
  {{- cart.item_count -}}
</span>
